{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03564",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.54,
      "end_seconds": 4.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "morning, doctor. Lovely to to meet you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.78,
      "end_seconds": 10.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.9,
      "end_seconds": 18.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "um, so... back pain that doesn't go away that's why I came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.56,
      "end_seconds": 21.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.37,
      "end_seconds": 25.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "About... well, about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.69,
      "end_seconds": 33.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.61,
      "end_seconds": 40.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "It It happens all the time. I'd call it mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.04,
      "end_seconds": 52.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.0,
      "end_seconds": 64.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.44,
      "end_seconds": 86.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "okay: heart rate 91, temperature 39.0, BP is 111 over 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.27,
      "end_seconds": 88.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.97,
      "end_seconds": 92.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.81,
      "end_seconds": 98.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.03,
      "end_seconds": 100.02,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "of course"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.53,
      "end_seconds": 102.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.98,
      "end_seconds": 126.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "there is a soft heart murmur you've not had before and a small tender spot on the fingertip"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.35,
      "end_seconds": 134.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.7,
      "end_seconds": 155.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "A few quick ones: breathlessness or high fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.18,
      "end_seconds": 160.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "no, no breathlessness or high fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.56,
      "end_seconds": 167.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any leg weakness or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.95,
      "end_seconds": 171.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.97,
      "end_seconds": 174.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.08,
      "end_seconds": 183.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "no, that's all fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.22,
      "end_seconds": 186.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Right, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.17,
      "end_seconds": 189.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.18,
      "end_seconds": 194.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.94,
      "end_seconds": 200.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.04,
      "end_seconds": 202.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.1,
      "end_seconds": 226.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.06,
      "end_seconds": 230.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "It's metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.22,
      "end_seconds": 233.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.09,
      "end_seconds": 240.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.56,
      "end_seconds": 243.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.34,
      "end_seconds": 252.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.85,
      "end_seconds": 260.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "So, do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.9,
      "end_seconds": 268.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Years back I got wheezing from diclofenac, so I stay away from it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.66,
      "end_seconds": 277.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, this is probably possible infection of the heart valve causing back and general symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.49,
      "end_seconds": 315.33,
      "duration_seconds": 21.84,
      "text": "Let's book blood cultures to look into possible endocarditis. This is not an ordinary back strain, so I want tests today. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. The medical admissions unit would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.13,
      "end_seconds": 321.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "alright, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.48,
      "end_seconds": 339.81,
      "duration_seconds": 16.33,
      "text": "keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency i'd like to see you again straight away have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.25,
      "end_seconds": 343.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}